### Verdict: REFUTED

### Justification
The claim that medical professionals deliberately cut the umbilical cord immediately to deny babies natural immunity and create a market for vaccination is unsupported by any evidence gathered. Immediate cord clamping historically became standard in the 1960s-70s based on clinical beliefs about reducing maternal hemorrhage risk ([myexpertmidwife.com](https://myexpertmidwife.com/blogs/my-expert-midwife/delayed-cord-clamping)), not any conspiratorial motive. While delayed cord clamping does provide measurable benefits—including ~80-100ml of additional blood, increased iron stores, and transfer of antibodies and stem cells ([Italian Journal of Pediatrics](https://ijponline.biomedcentral.com/articles/10.1186/s13052-020-00835-2); [Cochrane Review](https://www.cochrane.org/CD004074/PREG_effect-timing-umbilical-cord-clamping-term-infants-mother-and-baby-outcomes))—medical guidelines from WHO and ACOG have evolved based on accumulating scientific evidence of these health benefits ([ACOG](https://www.acog.org/womens-health/experts-and-stories/ask-acog/what-is-delayed-cord-clamping); [Birth Injury Help Center](https://www.birthinjuryhelpcenter.org/delayed-cord-clamping.html)), with no reference whatsoever to financial or vaccination-related motives. Peer-reviewed research on immunological outcomes found only short-term changes in lymphocyte subgroups with no difference in sepsis rates ([PMC study](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC6408182/)), and no source documents any intent by medical professionals to undermine infant immunity to justify vaccination.